WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.080
In an extraordinary move, the United States
is pursuing full diplomatic relations with

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:11.190
Cuba, but this won't mean the end to the economic
embargo, which only Congress can fully remove.

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:15.230
It's a comprehensive set of economic sanctions
on Cuba that has existed since roughly 1962.

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:19.750
It has been an absolute disaster for both
the United States and Cuba. Here are 7 reasons

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:24.160
why the embargo needs to end. #1. American
diplomats in Havana admit that the embargo

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:28.699
is a failure. The goal of the embargo was
to put pressure on the Cuban government -- economic

00:00:28.699 --> 00:00:32.269
pressure that was supposed to create popular
anger and resistance to the government and

00:00:32.269 --> 00:00:37.690
eventually overthrow it. But, according to
a 2009 cable from the U.S.'s top diplomat

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:43.030
in Havana at the time, that has failed to
happen. 2. Sanctions have failed to ruin Cuba's

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:49.170
economy. Cuba has seen a fair amount of economic
growth since the sanctions were created, indicating

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:53.000
that there wasn't nearly enough pressure to
send the economy into a full tailspin and

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:59.570
thus foment rebellion. #3. The embargo has
probably killed Cubans. The 1992 Cuba Democracy

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:03.920
Act restricted the flow of medical goods into
Cuba from the United States. This resulted

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:10.820
in a precipitous decline in access to medical
supplies inside Cuba. According to a 2010

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:15.200
review by two Stanford researchers, they believe
that the lack of access to this medicine was

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:20.920
responsible for several disease outbreaks
in the country, including an increase in Tuberculosis

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:25.990
fatalities. 4.) The embargo has not significantly
reduced Cuba's human rights abuses. Cuba has

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:30.170
a terrible human rights record. Among other
things, it's one of the worst countries on

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:33.960
freedom of the press in the Western Hemisphere,
and it throws dissidents and bloggers into

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:39.380
jail merely for criticizing the regime. However,
there's zero evidence that the sanctions regime

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:45.340
has done anything to make those abuses better.
5.) Almost the entire world opposes the United

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:50.310
States's policy. For 23 years, the United
Nations has voted to condemn the American

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:58.740
policy towards Cuba. The last vote in 2014
saw 188 out of 193 UN member states opposing

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:03.340
it in the General Assembly. 6.) Cuba is not
a state sponsor of terrorism anymore. Some

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.180
of the sanctions on Cuba come from the U.S.
designated Cuba a state sponsor of terrorism

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:13.250
because of its support for the Basque terrorist
group ETA and the Columbian group, the FARC.

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:18.270
Now, according to the State Department's most
recent review, there's no evidence that Cuba

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:23.890
is providing material military support to
these groups. Moreover, Cuba is cooperating

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:29.370
with Spain on the transfer of ETA prisoners,
and it has been sponsoring a peace conference

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:34.150
in Havana for the FARC and the Columbian government
-- one that appears to have resulted in a

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:39.220
unilateral ceasefire declaration by the FARC.
7.) A majority of Americans support normalizing

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:44.000
diplomatic relations with Cuba and majorities
support relaxing major parts of the embargo,

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.750
including restrictions on US companies doing
business in Cuba. Now, Cuban-Americans also

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:53.099
appear to oppose the embargo. If the people
who have the most reasons to hate the Castro

00:02:53.099 --> 00:02:57.399
government have come around to thinking the
embargo isn't worth the costs, 

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.420
it's time to reconsider the policy.

